=== p2-windows · W7 · page:automations/AutomationList (WinUI 3 / Fluent) ===
Parity unit : page:automations/AutomationList   kind=page   web route=/automations/list
Web source  : web/src/features/automations/pages/AutomationListPage.tsx
ADR refs    : ADR-002, ADR-004, ADR-005, ADR-006, ADR-011, ADR-013, ADR-014, ADR-015
Runner      : .NET 10.0.300 SDK present (dotnet --version 10.0.300) — NOT blocked.

=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection,
  unit-tested headlessly), <Name>.Source.cs (the generated-client feed), <Name>.ViewModel.cs
  (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view), exactly as the sibling W7
  ApiLogsPage / FeedbackQueuePage / SchemaDriftPage / VehicleCostPage do. The generated prompt's idealized
  "AutomationListPage.xaml + AutomationListPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/Automations" is mapped onto these
  real conventions; the surface registers itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by route name ("AutomationList",
  already in RouteTable.cs L123 → /automations/list) via ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data binding (ADR-004): the manifest data sources are useAutomations (GET /automations) and
  useBulkAutomationsUpdate (POST /automations/bulk). The view-model reads the list through an injected
  IAutomationListFeed; the default EmptyAutomationListFeed resolves the empty state, and the generated-client-backed
  AutomationListClientFeed (AutomationListPage.Source.cs) binds to the generated OpenAPI operations
  get_api_v1_automations (list) and post_api_v1_automations_bulk (bulk), posting the {ids, op} body exactly as the
  web hook does (op wire string enable|disable|delete via AutomationListRegistration.Wire; JSON property names pinned
  via [JsonPropertyName] so the wire shape is policy-independent), asserted in tests via the FakeApiClient. Both
  operations are confirmed in the generated apps/windows/Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs and the Go routes in
  internal/api/automation/crud.go (List → writeJSON([]automationResponse)) + internal/api/automation/bulk.go
  (BulkUpdate → apibulk.OperationResult {updated?,deleted?,failed:[{id,reason}]}). No HTTP touches the view.
- The list wire shape is a bare JSON array (the base models.Automation embedded in automationResponse:
  id/name/description?/enabled, no execution_count on the base row → tolerant parse reads execution_count as 0,
  matching the web a.execution_count ?? 0); AutomationListSnapshot.FromJson accepts both the bare array and the
  platform {data:[…]} envelope so the response round-trips losslessly.
- The web page renders its states INSIDE the GlassPanel (PageContainer only carries title/subtitle), so the native
  port reproduces them as visible Fluent regions per ADR-006: loading → three TsSkeleton bars (web three Skeleton
  h-10 bars, space-y-2 p-4); error → TsErrorDisplay (web ErrorDisplay) + Retry → RefreshAsync; empty → TsEmptyState
  (web EmptyState) "No automations yet" + the "Open builder" CTA (web actionTo /automations/new, raised through the
  page NavigationRequested event the shell wires to NavigateTo); success → the bulk-selectable table (master + per-row
  TsCheckbox, the name TsButton link to /automations/{id}, description, run count and the enabled/disabled TsBadge
  status chip). GlassPanel1 is always present; only its body switches — never a blank region.
- Bulk-selection + bulk-ops parity (web useBulkSelection + BulkActionToolbar + useBulkAutomationsUpdate): the
  view-model owns the selection set with toggle / toggleAll (master tri-state none/some/all via
  AutomationListProjection.ComputeMasterState) / clear, and RunBulkAsync runs an allowlisted op then — on success —
  clears the selection and reloads the list (web onSuccess invalidate + sel.clear()); on failure the selection is
  preserved so the user can retry (web onError toast). The Delete action routes through a destructive TsConfirmDialog
  (web ConfirmDialog) before mutating.
- SI units N/A (no unit-bearing physical fields on this surface — id, name, description, run count, enabled only);
  the run count renders as a plain integer (no grouping) to match the web {a.execution_count} JSX numeric render.
- 4 of the 22 manifest i18n keys were missing and added verbatim (web key names) to Strings/en/Resources.resw as
  translation.automationList.subtitle, translation.automationList.empty.body,
  translation.automationList.bulk.deleteConfirm.title and translation.automationList.bulk.deleteConfirm.body,
  alphabetically placed among the existing translation.automationList.* entries; the other 18 keys
  (automationList.* + bulk.selectAll/selectRow + common.delete/disabled/enabled) were already present. The surface
  resolves every label through the ILocalizer facade (extra non-counted keys error.loadFailed / common.retry /
  common.cancel / bulk.clear / bulk.selected are resolved too so no literal is hardcoded). The ar/he catalogs lag en
  by design; the app falls back to the English default via ILocalizer until translated.
- The Microsoft.UI-free Model/Source/ViewModel links were added to TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj (the bare WinUI view
  is excluded — it uses Microsoft.UI). The new files were authored with CRLF by the editor and normalized to LF via
  `dotnet format` so the lint gate's ENDOFLINE rule is satisfied.

